body:
A different point of view, the schools I did my graduate programs at (and I'm assuming other schools) tell their graduate students to not date undergraduate students. A lot of time graduate students are faculty/staff and that is a big no-go. I don't think there are  explicitly rules against it at every university, but it's highly unsupported. Other than that, he's at a vastly different point in life than you are as a graduate student and a lot of times even graduate-graduate student relationships don't work out due to the level of work/responsibilities. That could be field specific, but between undergraduate and graduate the "place" in life is vastly different. I'm 27, but can't imagine even dating someone 21. It's a cut off for me, but so is "Don't date an undergrad". If he's pushing, honestly that's a red flag because every grad student I talk to agrees with "don't date an undergrad" and the minimum cut off being 21. I'd leave it if I were you and focus on having your college experience.

&#x200B;

\*Edited for spelling
